Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "What each member of the company makes of the dale, by what they are: the cleric at the font, the ranger on the crest, the warrior at the cart, the thief at the door.".

  // The preset party is not a set of declared people, so it has no Remarks of its own. What a rule can ask of a member
  // is their calling, and print their name. Said once for the company, by whoever it has of the calling; a company
  // without a ranger has nobody to notice the cut saplings, and must notice them itself.
  Relation heardFont(group). Relation heardCrest(group). Relation heardCart(group). Relation heardDoor(group).
  Relation heardOx(group). Relation heardWheel(group).
  Relation quarrelled(group).

  Rule voice_font at nave when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, nave) and not heardFont(party)
    says "{?m} lays a hand flat on the font and keeps it there. 'Nobody tallies sins on a floor,' {?m} says, low. 'A tally has no use for a floor. This one has a high-water mark that somebody kept level with the roof-beam.'" {
    Assert heardFont(party).
  }
  Rule voice_crest at crest when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, crest) and not heardCrest(party)
    says "{?m} goes down on one knee by a stump and runs a finger across the cut. 'Same height, same angle, every one, all the way along,' {?m} says. 'That is not a man's hook, and it is not a deer. It is a thing with a very long reach and no hurry at all.'" {
    Assert heardCrest(party).
  }
  Rule voice_cart at yard when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, yard) and state(cart, covered) and not heardCart(party)
    says "{?m} walks round the cart once, looking at the axle and the gouged bed. 'That is not wool,' {?m} says. 'Something that weighs more than a man has been dragged in and out of there, and somebody has been at pains to hang a tarpaulin over the marks. Ask the foreman about his arm before you ask anyone about the hill.'" {
    Assert heardCart(party).
  }
  Rule voice_door at cellar when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, cellar) and not heardDoor(party)
    says "{?m} runs a thumb round the hinge of the new door in the old wall. 'Greased this week,' {?m} says. 'Somebody goes in and out of here, and not to roll barrels.'" {
    Assert heardDoor(party).
  }
  Rule voice_ox at taproom when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, taproom) and not heardOx(party)
    says "{?m} sits a while with an ear turned to the room. 'Everyone has a different story of the Mower and the same one of the steward,' {?m} says at last. 'When a village agrees about a man and not about a ghost, I know which one it has seen.'" {
    Assert heardOx(party).
  }
  Rule voice_wheel at sluice when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) and awake(?m) and at(party, sluice) and not heardWheel(party)
    says "{?m} stands with a palm held an inch from the nearest tooth of green bronze. 'No working in it,' {?m} says, puzzled. 'Nothing I could name. It does not do a thing. It counts, and the counting does the thing.'" {
    Assert heardWheel(party).
  }

  // A disagreement the company has with itself: only a company with both a warrior and a cleric has it, and each is right.
  // The money is forty crowns; the Hall owes the warrior's trade nothing; the cleric has seen the font.
  Rule quarrel_over_bounty at green when memberOf(?w, party) and hasCalling(?w, calling_warrior) and awake(?w)
    and memberOf(?c, party) and hasCalling(?c, calling_cleric) and awake(?c) and at(party, green) and knows(party, bounty_known) and knows(party, notches_known)
    and not paidBounty(venn) and not quarrelled(party)
    says "{?w} says it first, because somebody must. 'Forty crowns is forty crowns. It walks the crest at night and it has hit a man; lay it and be paid.' {?c} does not raise a voice. 'It keeps the wall that keeps the lake that keeps the chapel dry,' says {?c}. 'I would like to be certain what it is before I put a bar under its chin.' Neither looks at you, and both are waiting for you to say which of them is right." {
    Assert quarrelled(party).
  }

  // Taking a side is a choice with a cost: the warrior's way buys a man, the cleric's way wakes a priest, and neither
  // does the other's work. One answer closes the other.
  Relation sidedWarrior(group). Relation sidedCleric(group).
  Action side_warrior(actor: group, site: place, w: member, c: member) "Tell {c} that {w} is right about the forty crowns, and go to the foreman" {
    Description "Forty crowns and a man at the Hall who will not be paid. {w} will go in with the first of the money.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and quarrelled(party) and not sidedWarrior(party) and not sidedCleric(party)
      and memberOf(w, actor) and hasCalling(w, calling_warrior) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert sidedWarrior(party). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(dunnet, gold) by 3. Assert promisedDoor(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn). }
    Result "{c} says nothing, and goes on saying nothing all the way up the Hall lane. {w} finds Dunnet in the yard and puts three coin in his hand without a word of explanation, as a man pays a debt to his own trade. Dunnet counts them twice. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark,' he says, low. 'For you.' Behind you {c} has stopped at the gate and is looking at the hill with an expression you will remember at the wrong moment.".
  }
  Action side_cleric(actor: group, site: place, w: member, c: member) "Tell {w} that {c} is right, and take the font to Mother Ysolt" {
    Description "{c} will say what the notches are, in the chapel, before the parish; {w} will hold the door.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and quarrelled(party) and not sidedWarrior(party) and not sidedCleric(party)
      and memberOf(w, actor) and hasCalling(w, calling_warrior) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric) and knows(actor, notches_known).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert sidedCleric(party). Assert convinced(ysolt). }
    Result "{w} says nothing against it, which is not the same as agreeing, and stands at the chapel door with arms folded while {c} puts a hand on the font and says what the notches are, in the plain voice of someone who has done it before. Mother Ysolt listens to the end. When {c} has finished she looks up at the roof-beam, and then at {w}, and says: 'Ring the bell, if it comes. I will see it rung.' {w} unfolds arms. 'Forty crowns,' {w} says, to the doorpost, and goes out to see to the weather.".
  }
}
